Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 14:03:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/31] fix(verimark): include glib/gstdio.h for g_chmod /
 g_rename

The bootstrap atomic-write path uses g_chmod and g_rename to set
the sub1 file permissions and atomically replace the target. Both
live in glib/gstdio.h which wasn't included.

Drafted with AI assistance.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index 6b7810a..d0d46d0 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -45,6 +45,7 @@
 
 #include <gusb.h>
 #include <gio/gio.h>
+#include <glib/gstdio.h>   /* g_chmod, g_rename */
 #include <string.h>
 #include <time.h>
 
